	regionKind = "zone",
	kind = "region",
	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[Durotar is the homeland of the orcs, a red and broken country on the eastern shore of {link:kalimdor}Kalimdor{/link}. Its soil is cracked and dry, its canyons are sharp, and the sun beats down upon it without mercy. The orcs chose it gladly, for its harsh beauty reminds them of the world they lost. Here the Warchief {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} has raised his capital of {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link}, and here the young of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} are tested before they are sent out into the world. It is a land at peace only in name. Enemies watch it from the sea, from the canyons and from the shadows of its own caves.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[Before the orcs came, these lands were counted part of {link:the-barrens}The Barrens{/link}, and the {link:quilboar}quilboar{/link} of the {link:razormane-quilboar}Razormane tribe{/link} roamed them freely. After the {link:battle-of-mount-hyjal}Battle of Mount Hyjal{/link}, {link:thrall}Thrall{/link} led his people east to the coast and claimed the land between the Southfury River and the sea. He named it Durotar, in honor of his father, Durotan, chieftain of the {link:frostwolf-clan}Frostwolf clan{/link}. The {link:tauren}tauren{/link} and the {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear trolls{/link} lent their strength to the new nation, and the orcs drove the Razormane from all but the western edges of the land.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[Durotar is the heart of the new {link:horde}Horde{/link}. Yet its peace is thin. The humans of {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link} still hold the ruins of {link:tiragarde-keep}Tiragarde Keep{/link} on the eastern coast. The witch doctor {link:zalazane}Zalazane{/link} rules the {link:echo-isles}Echo Isles{/link} through dark voodoo. The {link:razormane-quilboar}Razormane{/link} press in from the west, the {link:kolkar-centaurs}Kolkar{/link} {link:centaurs}centaur{/link} plot in their crag, and the Dustwind {link:harpies}harpies{/link} prey upon the caravans. Worst of all, the cultists of the {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link} hide in the caves of Durotar, close to the gates of the capital itself. Of late, even the {link:naga}naga{/link} have been seen along the northern shore.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The orcs.{/b} They farm the hard ground, keep watch from {link:razor-hill}Razor Hill{/link} and train their young in the {link:valley-of-trials}Valley of Trials{/link}.
• {b}The {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} trolls.{/b} Driven from their islands, they have built a fishing village on the southern coast and wait for the day they can go home.
• {b}The goblins.{/b} Traders from {link:ratchet}Ratchet{/link} run caravans along the roads.
• {b}The {link:razormane-quilboar}Razormane quilboar{/link}.{/b} They cling to their bramble camps in the west and vow to take the land back.
• {b}The humans of {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link}.{/b} Sailors and marines who serve the memory of their dead admiral.
• {b}The {link:burning-blade}Burning Blade{/link}.{/b} Demon worshippers hiding in the caves.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The Landing.{/b} After the war against the {link:burning-legion}Burning Legion{/link}, the orcs built {link:orgrimmar}Orgrimmar{/link} and began to tame the land around it.
• {b}The Admiral's War.{/b} Soon after, Grand Admiral {link:daelin-proudmoore}Daelin Proudmoore{/link} sailed from {link:kul-tiras}Kul Tiras{/link} with a great fleet, determined to finish the orcs. His men raised {link:tiragarde-keep}Tiragarde Keep{/link} on the coast. The keep fell, and the admiral himself died before the walls of {link:theramore-isle}Theramore{/link}.
• {b}The Traitor of the Isles.{/b} The {link:darkspear-trolls}Darkspear{/link} settled the {link:echo-isles}Echo Isles{/link}, but one of their own witch doctors, {link:zalazane}Zalazane{/link}, turned his magic against them and drove the free trolls to the mainland.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Red Land",
			text = [=[• Aspiring shaman of the {link:horde}Horde{/link} drink a sacred draught called a sapta at {link:spirit-rock}Spirit Rock{/link}, high above the {link:valley-of-trials}Valley of Trials{/link}, and there they stand before the spirit of the earth.
• The wreckage of Proudmoore's fleet still lies in the shallows east of {link:tiragarde-keep}Tiragarde Keep{/link}. The orcs of {link:razor-hill}Razor Hill{/link} send swimmers to search it for human tools.
• A mother at Tor'kren Farm waited many days for her son, who had gone to hunt the crocolisks of the Southfury River. He did not come back.]=],
		},
	},
})

